From 535c59993a52cd86859240bf983caaa3e077035f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Oursland <jacob.oursland@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:11:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 149/202] Gui: Close combo popup on the closeEditor() teardown
 path

The enum QComboBox popup UAF has one more destroyer that the previous fixes
missed. releaseEditorFocus() now closes the drop-down on the model-reset
(buildUp) and row-removal paths, but the normal enum-editing teardown goes
through PropertyEditor::closeEditor() -> closePersistentEditor(), which frees
the combo directly and never closed its popup.

When the auto-opened drop-down is still open as closeEditor() runs (commit /
focus-out), the popup window is freed without Qt's closePopup() teardown. A
queued window-system mouse release is then delivered to the dead popup and
routed back into QComboBoxPrivate::itemSelected() on the dangling combo box,
crashing with EXC_BAD_ACCESS in doActivate() <- emitCurrentIndexChanged()
(sender = freed QComboBox), with no FreeCAD frames on the stack.

Close the popup with hidePopup() while the combo is still alive, right before
closePersistentEditor(), mirroring the releaseEditorFocus() guard on the other
teardown paths.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (claude-opus-4-8)
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp b/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
index 2f81f7ae8..2874eaa5d 100644
--- a/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
+++ b/src/Gui/propertyeditor/PropertyEditor.cpp
@@ -332,6 +332,12 @@ void PropertyEditor::closeEditor()
     if (editingIndex.isValid()) {
         Base::StateLocker guard(closingEditor);
         bool hasFocus = activeEditor && activeEditor->hasFocus();
+
+        // closePersistentEditor() below destroys the editor; close an open combo
+        // drop-down first so Qt tears the popup down normally (see releaseEditorFocus()).
+        if (auto* combo = qobject_cast<QComboBox*>(activeEditor.data())) {
+            combo->hidePopup();
+        }
 #ifdef Q_OS_MACOS
         // Brute-force workaround for https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/issues/14350
         int currentIndex = 0;
